/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  column22_wide_boiling_retry
  ===========================

  Toluene recovered from n-hexadecane (a solvent-from-heavy-oil split): 20
  stages, feed on 10, reflux ratio 3, distillate 50 of the 100 kmol/h fed, at
  1 atm, the feed a cold liquid at 300 K.  Solved by `model simultaneous;`.

  Pedagogical point: THE STARTING PROFILE CAN DECIDE WHETHER A COLUMN SOLVES.
  The unit's default start is a straight line from T_feed - 5 K at the top to
  T_feed + 15 K at the bottom, here 295 -> 315 K, while the column really runs
  from 384 K to 560 K.  Newton from that start stops after 80 iterations with
  |F| = 0.053 (relative volatilities of about 270 between the two components
  leave the stage equations nearly flat far from the answer).  The unit
  therefore retries, ANNOUNCED in the log and as an advisory, from a profile
  built from the package's own equilibrium (Theory Guide, `sec:column-thermo-seed`):
  the feed's bubble point (410 K) and dew point (531 K), relative volatilities
  at the bubble point, a Fenske-like split that honours the declared
  distillate rate, each stage at the bubble point of its own liquid
  (384 -> 560 K).  The same equations converge in 8 iterations.  The verdict is
  the model's own residual: a retry never swaps in another model.

  Two ways to read it.  (1) Run the case as shipped and read the
  `[solver] column ... did NOT converge; it was re-solved ...` line.  (2) Add
  `seed thermodynamic;` to the operation block: the column then starts from
  the profile and the retry never happens.

  Expected: T_top ~ 383.8 K, T_bottom ~ 559.7 K (toluene and n-hexadecane's
  normal boiling points, because both products are nearly pure).  The CMO
  reboiler duty is far above the column's own energy envelope (printed
  beside it): with latent heats this different, constant molal overflow is
  not a good model, which is what `model fullMESH;` is for.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        column22;
        type        distillationColumn;
        model       simultaneous;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( distillate  bottoms );

        operation
        {
            nStages        20;
            feedStage      10;
            refluxRatio    3.0;
            distillateRate 50.0 kmol/h;
            // feedQuality deleted (C169): the CMO q is the stream's, from its
            // enthalpy -- a declared 1.0 contradicted this subcooled feed.
            P              1.01325 bar;
        }
    }
);
